diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index 160025a..e7462ac 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -172,6 +172,9 @@ rather than using `@work-leaf` read, patch, or lock directives.
 
 - `AgentBackend::launch` starts an agent session from an `AgentLaunch`.
 - `AgentBackend::send` sends a prompt to an existing agent session.
+- `AgentBackend::command` executes a backend-native command against an existing session. The default
+  implementation returns an unsupported-command assistant message without sending a model request,
+  so providers opt into native command execution only when they have a command protocol to expose.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming` and `AgentBackend::send_streaming` provide real-time output to a
   sink of `AgentStreamEvent` values. Their default implementations call the non-streaming methods.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming_interruptible` and
@@ -306,6 +309,8 @@ The primary public methods are:
   `launch_prepared_agent_streaming_with_ids` for UI-driven launch flows.
 - `CommandChat::send_to_agent`, `send_to_agent_streaming`, and
   `send_to_agent_streaming_with_ids` for UI-driven message flows.
+- `CommandChat::send_agent_command` for UI-driven backend command flows such as selected-agent
+  slash commands.
 - `CommandChat::shutdown_agents` and `shutdown_handle` for lifecycle cleanup.
 
 `CommandChat` uses the active `AgentProfile` when launching user agents, reviewers, and linearizers.
@@ -654,9 +659,11 @@ New agent-provider support follows this path:
 1. Define an `AgentProfile` with `AgentKind::External`.
 2. Implement `AgentBackend` for the provider.
 3. Override streaming methods when the provider can emit real-time output.
-4. Return an `AgentShutdownHandle` when the provider owns child processes.
-5. Pass the profile through `CommandChat::with_agent_profile`.
-6. Use `WorkLeafController` or `CommandChat` without modifying terminal UI code.
+4. Override `AgentBackend::command` when the provider supports backend-native commands that should
+   be reachable from selected-agent slash input.
+5. Return an `AgentShutdownHandle` when the provider owns child processes.
+6. Pass the profile through `CommandChat::with_agent_profile`.
+7. Use `WorkLeafController` or `CommandChat` without modifying terminal UI code.
 
 `AgentBackend::session` is an optional session snapshot hook. Work Leaf tracks hidden system-agent
 initialization itself, so provider implementations do not need to override `session` for persistent
